{"title":"1982 AHSME Problems/Problem 26","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_26\">Problem 26</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 26\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> representation of a perfect square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e77847508170126603618bb34389391d63ca3db4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab3c$\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296eacc72cb179258b4140b7ac9981ec88964fe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\ne 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> equals \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/0/fb00973be29fc597ae05cee103d869de1110e7dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)} 0\\qquad  \\text{(B)}1 \\qquad  \\text{(C)} 3\\qquad  \\text{(D)} 4\\qquad  \\text{(E)} \\text{not uniquely determined}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"472\" height=\"17\" />    \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A perfect square will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/b/29bf2ba71ce24b3dfad699892beb6911e1ed9b64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(8k+r)^2=64k^2+16kr+r^2\\equiv r^2\\pmod{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"349\" height=\"19\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/0/22020d306b55a84d18e1af58b934d0bf51dd3797.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=0,1,...,7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9fe6de05d4299e5a5ca5921688f3b6c3caab8ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2\\equiv 1,4,9,0 \\pmod{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e77847508170126603618bb34389391d63ca3db4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab3c$\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> in base 8 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/6/e2644f79a7a9823c5052bf16209fddffae5a45ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a8^3+b8^2+3(8)+c\\equiv 8+c\\pmod{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"300\" height=\"19\" />. It being a perfect square means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a3756005125c11ee16ce9cc7a504681a800d0d94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8+c\\equiv 1,4,9,0 \\pmod{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"207\" height=\"20\" />. That means that c can only be 1 so the answer is 1 = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb6bca9b92973ac3a2a76aa67a5220e98ecc947f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"45\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><t